&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 8pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 8pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-weight: bold;"&gt;4.RELATED PARTY TRANSACTIONS&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 8pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-weight: bold; font-style: italic;"&gt;Operations and Maintenance Agreement.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-weight: bold; font-style: italic;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;On June 26, 2019, Double E and Summit Permian II entered into an Operations and Management Agreement, as amended ("OMA") relating to the operation of the Project. Summit Permian II will operate the pipeline upon commissioning of the Project in accordance with the terms of the OMA. The OMA may be terminated upon mutual written consent, upon the resignation of Summit Permian II or upon the removal of Summit Permian II in accordance with the provisions of the OMA.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 8pt;"&gt;Upon commissioning the pipeline in November 2021, Summit Permian II began receiving compensation under the OMA of approximately $0.3 million per month. During each of the years ended December 31, 2025 and 2024, Double E incurred $3.6 million of costs from Summit Permian II under the terms of the OMA, which is recorded within Operations Expense in the statement of income.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 8pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-weight: bold;"&gt;5.SUBSEQUENT EVENTS&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 8pt;"&gt;The Company has reviewed and updated subsequent events through April 20, 2026, the date its financial statements were available to be issued. There were no subsequent events that required additional disclosure in the Company's financial statements, except for the following.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="font-family: Calibri; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;In January of 2026, Double E executed an agreement which includes 210 MMcf/d of firm capacity on the Double E Pipeline, with the first tranche of volume set to begin flowing in the fourth quarter of 2026, and an 11-year term. Additionally, in February 2026, Double E executed an agreement which includes 230&amp;#160;MMcf/d of firm capacity on the Double E Pipeline, with the first tranche of volume set to begin flowing in the fourth quarter of 2027, and over an 11-year term.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:NotesToFinancialStatementsTextBlock>
